  "$comment": [
    "What each scorecard row rests on, in a form a check can read.",
    "`suites` names the run records under .evidence/ that must exist, must record exit 0, and",
    "must have been produced against the current commit. `specs` names the test files that",
    "carry the row's @acceptance marker; deleting one is then a failure rather than a row that",
    "quietly stays true. Prose belongs in scorecard.md; this file is the part a gate enforces.",
    "Governing: ENG-CI-001, ACC-DEMO-SMOKE. Owner: quality."
  ],
  "freshness": {
    "rule": "commit",
    "note": "A record counts only for the commit it names. Anything else \u2014 a record from an earlier commit, or none at all \u2014 fails the gate, because a suite that passed on other code is not evidence about this one. Uncommitted working-tree changes are not detected; the rule binds a record to HEAD, not to a tree hash."
  },
